{"id":"CVE-2024-7347","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"f5","published":"2024-08-14T14:32:33.913Z","updated":"2025-11-03T20:56:24.679Z","title":"NGINX MP4 module vulnerability","description":"NGINX Open Source and NGINX Plus have a vulnerability in the ngx_http_mp4_module, which might allow an attacker to over-read NGINX worker memory resulting in its termination, using a specially crafted mp4 file. The issue only affects NGINX if it is built with the ngx_http_mp4_module and the mp4 directive is used in the configuration file. Additionally, the attack is possible only if an attacker can trigger the processing of a specially crafted mp4 file with the ngx_http_mp4_module.  Note: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.","cwe":["CWE-126 CWE-126: Buffer Over-read"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":4.7,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"},{"src":"cna","v":"4.0","score":5.7,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Open Source","defaultStatus":"unknown","modules":["ngx_http_mp4_module"],"versions":["affected 1.5.13 <* (semver) changes:unaffected@1.26.2;unaffected@1.27.1"]},{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Plus","defaultStatus":"unknown","modules":["ngx_http_m4_module"],"versions":["affected R4 <* (custom) changes:unaffected@R31 P3;unaffected@R32 P1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K000140529","tags":["vendor-advisory"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2024/08/14/4"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/03/msg00017.html"}],"credits":["F5 acknowledges Nils Bars for bringing this issue to our attention and following the highest standards of coordinated disclosure."],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-7634","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"f5","published":"2024-08-22T18:07:31.058Z","updated":"2024-08-22T19:29:33.197Z","title":"NGINX Agent Vulnerability","description":"NGINX Agent's \"config_dirs\" restriction feature allows a highly privileged attacker to gain the ability to write/overwrite files outside of the designated secure directory.","cwe":["CWE-22 CWE-22 Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":4.9,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N"},{"src":"cna","v":"4.0","score":6.9,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Agent","defaultStatus":"unknown","modules":["Agent"],"versions":["affected 2.17.0 <2.37.0 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K000140630","tags":["vendor-advisory"]}],"credits":["F5"],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-7646","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2024-08-16T17:36:53.783Z","updated":"2024-08-19T18:28:09.677Z","description":"A security issue was discovered in ingress-nginx where an actor with permission to create Ingress objects (in the `networking.k8s.io` or `extensions` API group) can bypass annotation validation to inject arbitrary commands and obtain the credentials of the ingress-nginx controller. In the default configuration, that credential has access to all secrets in the cluster.","cwe":["CWE-20 CWE-20 Improper Input Validation"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":8.8,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"ingress-nginx","defaultStatus":"affected","versions":["affected 1.11.0 <1.11.2 (semver)","unaffected 1.11.2","unaffected 1.10.4","affected 0 <1.10.4 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"kubernetes","product":"ingress-nginx","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:kubernetes:ingress-nginx:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 1.11.0 <1.11.2 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"kubernetes","product":"ingress-nginx","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:kubernetes:ingress-nginx:1.11.2:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 1.11.2"]},{"vendor":"kubernetes","product":"ingress-nginx","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:kubernetes:ingress-nginx:1.10.4:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 1.10.4"]},{"vendor":"kubernetes","product":"ingress-nginx","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:kubernetes:ingress-nginx:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0 <1.10.4 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/126744","tags":["issue-tracking"]},{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/kubernetes-security-announce/c/a1__cKjWkfA","tags":["mailing-list"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/11719","tags":["patch"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/11721","tags":["patch"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2024/08/16/5"}],"credits":["André Storfjord Kristiansen"],"vendors":["kubernetes","nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-10318","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"f5","published":"2024-11-06T16:48:56.128Z","updated":"2024-11-06T16:57:40.692Z","title":"NGINX OpenID Connect Vulnerability","description":"A session fixation issue was discovered in the NGINX OpenID Connect reference implementation, where a nonce was not checked at login time. This flaw allows an attacker to fix a victim's session to an attacker-controlled account. As a result, although the attacker cannot log in as the victim, they can force the session to associate it with the attacker-controlled account, leading to potential misuse of the victim's session.","cwe":["CWE-384 CWE-384 Session Fixation"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.4,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"cna","v":"4.0","score":5.1,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX OpenID Connect","repo":"https://github.com/nginxinc/nginx-openid-connect/","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected fa1ad160e2637d1d583611124478039170d726ab <133504f4fd9f72f3e36668f9f2f3d32a86fcb269 (git)"]},{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Instance Manager","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 2.5.0 <2.17.4 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX API Connectivity Manager","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 1.0.0 <1.9.3 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Ingress Controller","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 1.0.0 <3.7.1 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K000148232","tags":["vendor-advisory"]}],"credits":["Christian August Holm Hansen of Binary Security AS"],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-22196","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2024-01-11T19:24:07.984Z","updated":"2025-06-17T21:09:16.453Z","title":"Authenticated (user role) SQL injection in `OrderAndPaginate` (GHSL-2023-270)","description":"Nginx-UI is an online statistics for Server Indicators​​ Monitor CPU usage, memory usage, load average, and disk usage in real-time. This issue may lead to information disclosure. By using `DefaultQuery`, the `\"desc\"` and `\"id\"` values are used as default values if the query parameters are not set. Thus, the `order` and `sort_by` query parameter are user-controlled and are being appended to the `order` variable without any sanitization. This issue has been patched in version 2.0.0.beta.9.\n\n","cwe":["CWE-89 CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:L"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"0xJacky","product":"nginx-ui","versions":["affected < 2.0.0.beta.9"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/security/advisories/GHSA-h374-mm57-879c","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/commit/ec93ab05a3ecbb6bcf464d9dca48d74452df8a5b","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-22197","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2024-01-11T17:56:11.865Z","updated":"2025-06-17T21:09:16.574Z","title":"Authenticated (user role) remote command execution by modifying `nginx` settings (GHSL-2023-269)","description":"Nginx-ui is online statistics for Server Indicators​​ Monitor CPU usage, memory usage, load average, and disk usage in real-time. The `Home > Preference` page exposes a small list of nginx settings such as `Nginx Access Log Path` and `Nginx Error Log Path`. However, the API also exposes `test_config_cmd`, `reload_cmd` and `restart_cmd`. While the UI doesn't allow users to modify any of these settings, it is possible to do so by sending a request to the API. This issue may lead to authenticated Remote Code Execution, Privilege Escalation, and Information Disclosure. This issue has been patched in version 2.0.0.beta.9.","cwe":["CWE-77 CWE-77: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7.7,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"0xJacky","product":"nginx-ui","versions":["affected < 2.0.0.beta.9"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/security/advisories/GHSA-pxmr-q2x3-9x9m","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/commit/827e76c46e63c52114a62a899f61313039c754e3","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-22198","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2024-01-11T19:38:27.296Z","updated":"2024-08-01T22:35:34.877Z","title":"Authenticated (user role) arbitrary command execution by modifying `start_cmd` setting (GHSL-2023-268)","description":"Nginx-UI is a web interface to manage Nginx configurations. It is vulnerable to arbitrary command execution by abusing the configuration settings. The `Home > Preference` page exposes a list of system settings such as `Run Mode`, `Jwt Secret`, `Node Secret` and `Terminal Start Command`. While the UI doesn't allow users to modify the `Terminal Start Command` setting, it is possible to do so by sending a request to the API. This issue may lead to authenticated remote code execution, privilege escalation, and information disclosure. This vulnerability has been patched in version 2.0.0.beta.9.","cwe":["CWE-77 CWE-77: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7.1,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"0xJacky","product":"nginx-ui","versions":["affected < 2.0.0.beta.9"]},{"vendor":"nginxui","product":"nginx_ui","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:nginxui:nginx_ui:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0 <2.0.0.beta.8 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"nginxui","product":"nginx_ui","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:nginxui:nginx_ui:2.0.0:beta9:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["unaffected 2.0.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/security/advisories/GHSA-8r25-68wm-jw35","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/commit/827e76c46e63c52114a62a899f61313039c754e3","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/blob/04bf8ec487f06ab17a9fb7f34a28766e5f53885e/api/system/settings.go#L18","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/blob/04bf8ec487f06ab17a9fb7f34a28766e5f53885e/api/terminal/pty.go#L11","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/blob/04bf8ec487f06ab17a9fb7f34a28766e5f53885e/internal/pty/pipeline.go#L29","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/blob/04bf8ec487f06ab17a9fb7f34a28766e5f53885e/router/middleware.go#L45","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/blob/04bf8ec487f06ab17a9fb7f34a28766e5f53885e/settings/server.go#L12","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-23827","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2024-01-29T16:07:13.953Z","updated":"2024-11-12T21:41:24.606Z","title":"Nginx-UI arbitrary file write through the Import Certificate feature","description":"Nginx-UI is a web interface to manage Nginx configurations. The Import Certificate feature allows arbitrary write into the system. The feature does not check if the provided user input is a certification/key and allows to write into arbitrary paths in the system. It's possible to leverage the vulnerability into a remote code execution overwriting the config file app.ini. Version 2.0.0.beta.12 fixed the issue.","cwe":["CWE-22 CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"0xJacky","product":"nginx-ui","versions":["affected < 2.0.0.beta.12"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/security/advisories/GHSA-xvq9-4vpv-227m","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-23828","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2024-01-29T16:49:51.440Z","updated":"2024-11-12T21:31:32.752Z","title":"Nginx-UI authenticated RCE through injecting into the application config via CRLF","description":"Nginx-UI is a web interface to manage Nginx configurations. It is vulnerable to an authenticated arbitrary command execution via CRLF attack when changing the value of test_config_cmd or start_cmd. This vulnerability exists due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2024-22197 and CVE-2024-22198. This vulnerability has been patched in version 2.0.0.beta.12.","cwe":["CWE-74 CWE-74: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":8.8,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"0xJacky","product":"nginx-ui","versions":["affected < v2.0.0.beta.12"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/0xJacky/nginx-ui/security/advisories/GHSA-qcjq-7f7v-pvc8","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2024-24989","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"f5","published":"2024-02-14T16:30:26.081Z","updated":"2025-05-12T15:07:40.892Z","title":"NGINX HTTP/3 QUIC vulnerability","description":"When NGINX Plus or NGINX OSS are configured to use the HTTP/3 QUIC module, undisclosed requests can cause NGINX worker processes to terminate.\n\nNote: The HTTP/3 QUIC module is not enabled by default and is considered experimental. For more information, refer to  Support for QUIC and HTTP/3 https://nginx.org/en/docs/quic.html .\n\n\n\nNOTE: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated","cwe":["CWE-476 CWE-476 NULL Pointer Dereference"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Plus","defaultStatus":"unknown","modules":["HTTP/3","QUIC"],"versions":["affected R31 <R31 P1 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"F5","product":"NGINX Open Source","defaultStatus":"unknown","modules":["HTTP/3","QUIC"],"versions":["affected 1.25.3 <1.25.4 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K000138444","tags":["vendor-advisory"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2024/05/30/4"}],"credits":["F5"],"vendors":["nginx"]}
